# credential-bindings.yaml -- operator-gated trust-boundary config for the credential
# broker (deploy/credential-use.ps1; design brief
# harness-v3.0/specs/credential-broker-design-brief-2026-07-23.md). Same family as
# deploy/origin-config.yaml and deploy/signing-config.yaml -- read that pair's headers
# first; this file's doctrine is theirs, restated for a new trust boundary.
#
# GOVERNS: which DESTINATION patterns each named credential may be used against.
# credential-use loads this file, and a call whose (name, destination) pair is not
# explicitly bound here REFUSES -- naming why. This is the injection defense: a steered
# session holding `credential-use` capability cannot point an existing, already-stored
# credential at a new destination, because the destination set is pinned here,
# out-of-band, by the operator -- never by anything a session writes.
#
# FAIL-SAFE DEFAULT (identical doctrine to origin-config.yaml / signing-config.yaml):
# this file ABSENT, unreadable, not in the EXACT documented shape below, or ANY single
# entry structurally invalid (bad name charset, missing `destinations:`, an empty
# destinations list, a malformed quoted scalar, an unrecognised key, a duplicate
# `name:`) -- ALL of these degrade the ENTIRE bindings set to EMPTY. Every
# credential-use call then refuses, for every name, unconditionally. A partially-
# honored trust config is worse than an honestly empty one: this file ships EMPTY, on
# purpose, so a fresh instance is fail-safe by default rather than fail-open by
# omission.
#
# THIS FILE IS AN OPERATOR-GATED TRUST-CONTROL SURFACE (ROUTE-1-style note, mirroring
# origin-config.yaml's and signing-config.yaml's own convention): adding a binding here
# decides which destinations a named credential may be delivered to. Treat edits as an
# operator-authored, out-of-band change only -- NEVER something an agent/executor edits
# on its own initiative. A session that needs a new destination bound must ASK the
# operator to add the line; it must never add the line itself.
#
# NEVER BIND A FINANCIAL CREDENTIAL HERE. Banking, card, brokerage, crypto-exchange, and
# government-ID credentials are excluded from this broker by POLICY, held by the
# operator, not by anything this file or credential-use.ps1 can detect -- see the design
# brief's "Excluded entirely" section. credential-use.ps1 also carries a best-effort
# financial-domain denylist as defense-in-depth, but that denylist is honestly
# incomplete; do not treat its silence about a destination as permission to bind a
# financial credential.
#
# credential-use.ps1's parser for this file is DELIBERATELY MINIMAL AND STRICT --
# nothing beyond the exact shape below (no ConvertFrom-Yaml, no general YAML support;
# see credential-selftest.ps1's malformed-bindings cases for what "strict" means in
# practice). Strictness is the point: a shape the parser doesn't recognise must be
# malformed, never partially understood.
#
# Schema (top-level `bindings:` key, a list of entries, exactly this indentation):
#   bindings:
#     - name: <credential-name>            # matches the -Name a script stored/uses;
#                                           # charset: letters, digits, '.', '_', '-'
#       destinations: ["<glob-pattern>", "<glob-pattern>", ...]
#                                           # `*` is the only wildcard; matched against
#                                           # the whole -Destination string a session
#                                           # passes to credential-use, case-insensitive
#       rotates_at: <free text>            # OPTIONAL, documentation only, never
#                                           # enforced by code -- names where this
#                                           # credential rotates (report's rotation-
#                                           # playbook discipline: "each binding's
#                                           # comment names where that credential
#                                           # rotates")
#
# Example (NOT active -- shown for shape only; this file ships with an empty list):
#   bindings:
#     - name: acme-crm-admin
#       destinations: ["https://*.acme-crm.com/*"]
#       rotates_at: Acme CRM admin panel, Settings > Users > acme-crm-admin > Reset password

bindings: []
